Package: simcompR
Title: Block-Diagram Modeling and Dynamic System Simulation in R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Adam R", "Sophie", email = "adamrsophie@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: A code-first framework for building and simulating block
    diagrams of dynamic systems. Models are directed graphs of blocks with
    typed, sized input and output ports. Compilation validates connections
    and signal dimensions, analyzes direct-feedthrough dependencies,
    detects algebraic loops through strongly connected components (and can
    solve them with Newton iterations), and builds a deterministic,
    insertion-order invariant execution schedule. The runtime integrates
    continuous states with 'deSolve', advances discrete and multirate
    blocks on an exact integer-indexed sample clock with defined
    output-before-update semantics, restarts integration at scheduled
    discontinuities, and locates zero crossings for state resets, mode
    changes and terminal events. Hierarchical parameterized subsystems,
    Stateflow-like state machines, portable JSON model files, parameter
    sweeps and reproducible Monte Carlo experiments are included. The
    design is inspired by 'Simulink' and 'bdsim'
    <https://github.com/petercorke/bdsim>; no 'Python' or 'MATLAB' is
    required.
